{
  "_description": "Task manifest for generating learned-oracle training data. Superset of gistify_tasks.json: the same 6 scored benchmark tasks plus 12 train-only tasks that exist purely to produce more Phase 4b removal attempts.",
  "_split_semantics": "split='benchmark' rows come from the 6 tasks the oracle is later evaluated on; split='train_only' rows never appear in any scored run. Both are used for training, which makes the end-to-end benchmark number optimistic — the honest generalization estimate is the leave-one-repo-out CV reported by ml/oracle.py, where a fold trains on one repo and is scored on the other.",
  "_repo_choice": "Both repos are already in .gistify_repo_cache, so no new clone or install cost. Only two repos are available, which caps leave-one-repo-out at 2 folds — few, but honest. Leave-one-task-out was rejected: 4 of the 6 benchmark tasks share the requests repo, so per-task folds would train and test on the same files.",
  "_environment": "Runs under the pinned benchmark venv (pytest==9.0.0). flask 3.0.3's conftest uses _pytest.monkeypatch.notset, which pytest 9.1 removed; without the pin every flask task errors during collection and produces garbage rows.",
